      "role": "user",
      "content": "okay but that feels a bit one-sided. if i'm in a moot court, i need to know why the other side is actually valid. if i go with your suggestion, won't my opponent just argue that without broad privilege, the President can't get honest advice from advisors because they'll be too scared of subpoenas? don't you think the argument for a strong, expansive privilege is actually more legally sound in a modern context?",
